    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d115">

                <pb facs="0113" n="101" sameAs="frus:frus1942v04/pg101"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">124.84/157</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Under Secretary of State</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Welles</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Chief of the Division of Near Eastern
                        Affairs</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Murray</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1942-03-09">March 9, 1942</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Murray</hi>: I think Dr. Berle is right.<anchor
                        n="3" xml:id="d115-f1"/> My thought would be that if we have some
                    appropriate officer who can be spared in the Near East we could reopen our
                    mission in Addis Ababa with a Chargé d’Affaires.</p>
                <p>Please consult Dr. Berle and Mr. Shaw<anchor n="4" xml:id="d115-f2"/> and let me
                    have your joint recommendations so that I may take the matter up with the
                    President.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>S[<hi rendition="#small-caps">umner</hi>] W[<hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >elles</hi>]</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d115-f1" n="3" xml:id="d115-f1-content">
                <p>Attached to Mr. Murray’s memorandum, <hi rendition="#italic">supra</hi>, is a
                    handwritten notation by the Assistant Secretary of State, Adolf A. Berle, Jr.,
                    dated March 9, as follows: “I think we should promptly consider setting up
                    diplomatic representation at Addis Ababa”.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d115-f2" n="4" xml:id="d115-f2-content">
                <p>G. Howland Shaw, Assistant Secretary of State.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
